# Regression test: deeply recursive function produces E040 (DepthExceeded) not E070 (CircularDependency).
#
# Note: The original test used [@Int [call $f [call $+ $x 1]]] to exercise the ThunkState::Guarded
# path specifically. That form overflows even 128MB stacks in debug mode (each materialize() frame
# is large, and 256 levels × ~400KB = ~100MB). The @Int wrapper has been removed so the test fits
# in the corpus runner's stack budget.
#
# The Guarded-stuck-InProgress bug is covered by a dedicated unit test:
# eval.rs::tests::test_guarded_thunk_depth_exceeded_restores_state (line ~6820)
# That unit test directly verifies: (1) DepthExceeded returns Guarded state, not InProgress,
# (2) retry produces DepthExceeded again (not CircularDependency).
[f: [fn [x] [f [+ x 1]]]
 result: [f 0]]
=== out
[E040]
